    "title": "Opinion: I ran Shasta County's elections for 20 years. I know Trump's playbook - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Cathy Darling Allen ,\n6 hours ago\nThis opinion piece was submitted by former Shasta County Clerk and Registrar of Voters Cathy Darling Allen. Do you have an opinion to share? Find our guidelines here. For 20 years, the voters of Shasta County, California, trusted me to run their elections. They elected me county clerk and registrar of voters five times. Most recently, in 2022, I won nearly 70 percent of the vote in a county Donald Trump carried by more than 60%. My job was never to care who won. It was to make sure every eligible voter could cast a ballot and every ballot was counted accurately.\nRead full article\n1",
    "summary": "By Cathy Darling Allen , This opinion piece was submitted by former Shasta County Clerk and Registrar of Voters Cathy Darling Allen. For 20 years, the voters of Shasta County, California, trusted me to run their elections. They elected me county clerk and registrar of voters five times. Most recently, in 2022, I won nearly 70 percent of the vote in a county Donald Trump carried by more than 60%. It was to make sure every eligible voter could cast a ballot and every ballot was counted accurately.",
